WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:05.830
AMC's The Walking Dead has become a staple
of Sunday television, endlessly shocking and

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:09.420
delighting fans with its gory action and non-stop
drama.

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:14.519
The grim apocalyptic series has gotten increasingly
violent over the years, to the point that

00:00:14.519 --> 00:00:19.019
some fans have even called it quits because
of the alarming brutality, while others have

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:22.890
become irked by some key changes from the
original comic's scenes.

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:27.119
But even those who've stuck around from the
start still might be surprised to find out

00:00:27.119 --> 00:00:28.550
these facts about the series.

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:31.279
From on-set hijinks to spoiler maintenance
problems, here's what you may not know about

00:00:31.279 --> 00:00:32.880
The Walking Dead...

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:34.090
Taking the lead

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:39.130
In a major case of Hollywood sliding doors,
Andrew Lincoln almost wasn't cast as Sheriff

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:43.020
Rick Grimes because he'd accepted a role in
another film at the time.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:47.890
But life got in the way: his second child
was born shortly before the film was expected

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:52.130
to commence production, so Lincoln decided
against shooting it after all.

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:56.880
He told The Hollywood Reporter, "I got a friend
to replace me in this movie and the next day,

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:58.650
this script came through from AMC.

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:02.420
I must have been on their radar with Frank
[Darabont], and he wanted me to test.

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:03.620
It was incredible."

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:07.820
What got him to agree to take the audition
to begin with, he later revealed, was the

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:13.259
fact that executive producer and show co-creator
Frank Darabont was involved.

00:01:13.259 --> 00:01:16.909
He believed that meant the show could have
a real future that made moving his growing

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:18.189
family worth it.

00:01:18.189 --> 00:01:22.170
As he told Rolling Stone, "Frank talked us
into getting on that plane."

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:23.899
SWAT team swarm

00:01:23.899 --> 00:01:28.670
During production on the second episode of
the inaugural season, The Walking Dead's cast

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:32.869
and crew got an unexpected set of visitors:
a SWAT team.

00:01:32.869 --> 00:01:37.950
Mearle actor Michael Rooker was on a rooftop
shooting his rifle to simulate a zombie sniper

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:42.929
session, but onlookers mistook his behavior
for the real deal — and called in the cops.

00:01:42.929 --> 00:01:45.420
"I saw people jump and run.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:47.969
They had already dispatched the SWAT team.

00:01:47.969 --> 00:01:50.400
The officer said, 'Please, stand down.'"

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:54.340
It wasn't the last time a false alarm would
ring regarding the show.

00:01:54.340 --> 00:02:00.200
In 2016, a Great Falls, Montana, family found
themselves swarmed by police after neighbors

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:05.499
called in a possible domestic violence incident
involving guns inside their home … because

00:02:05.499 --> 00:02:09.340
they were watching the show loud enough for
neighbors to think a big shootout was going

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:10.500
down.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:11.810
Pulling pranks

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:16.720
For a show with such grisly material as The
Walking Dead, its stars sure know how to have

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:18.970
fun when the cameras aren't rolling.

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:24.560
Actor Norman Reedus in particular has a long-running
history of pranking Andrew Lincoln and others

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:25.560
during production.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:30.000
Some of his greatest hits from the thick history
book of their prank wars include Reedus filling

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.700
Lincoln's car vents with glitter so that it
exploded all over him as soon as he cranked

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:39.160
the A/C. Then there was the time he taught
Lincoln to greet Japanese fans with the phrase

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:43.920
"where's the toilet" when he wanted to say
"thank you for allowing me to be here."

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:48.850
Lincoln's been known to get him back on occasion,
too, like when he put Reedus' treasured motorcycle

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:53.130
on a boat with a sex doll and sent it sailing
to the middle of a lake.

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:56.210
But the best is when he gets more precise
forms of payback.

00:02:56.210 --> 00:02:57.860
"Believe me, this is the end.”

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:07.440
AMC Easter eggs

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:11.650
The Walking Dead is an Easter egg lover's
dream, because the show is filled with hidden

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:16.150
tributes to the original comics, other zombie
epics, and plenty more.

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:20.300
AMC's sister hit Breaking Bad received some
of the most clever winks and references.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:25.290
For instance, there was the Heisenberg-blue
meth that appeared in a bag of drugs shown

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:26.760
in the second season.

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:31.460
And let's not forget when Daryl Dixon basically
described his brother's dealer — and Jesse

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:33.660
Pinkman fit the description to a tee.

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:35.860
"Merle had this dealer.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:39.860
This janky little white guy.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:42.240
He says ‘I'm gonna kill you bitch.’”

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:46.100
The connections have been significant enough
to even inspire some theorists to connect

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:51.320
the timelines of the two shows and posit a
cause-and-effect relationship between Walter

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:54.780
White's chemical concoction and the onset
of the zombie plague.

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:55.780
"Yeah Mr. White.

00:03:55.780 --> 00:03:57.950
Yeah science!"

00:03:57.950 --> 00:03:59.460
Hey, anything's possible!

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:04.570
The Walking Dead has still yet to explain
where and why the walker infection happened.

00:04:04.570 --> 00:04:05.880
Irking the neighbors

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:10.410
You might think living in a small town where
one of TV's biggest hits is made would be

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:11.410
a treat.

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:16.090
But for some residents of Senoia, Georgia,
the experience of becoming a mini-Hollywood

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:17.900
has been unpleasant at times.

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:22.930
As reported by ABC News, some of Senoia's
natives have been annoyed by being asked to

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:28.130
change their activities in their hometown
as a result of its proximity to the set — from

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:33.260
taking pictures to trimming trees, show officials
have stepped in to moderate what would otherwise

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:35.660
be considered pretty ordinary behaviors.

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:42.130
"And they come out of there sayin’ I need
to stop, they’re filming.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:47.180
Uh, I said ‘Well no, you just carry your
happy butt right behind the wall.’”

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:51.870
Set attention has also spawned an army of
"Walker Stalkers" — that is, fans who case

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:56.820
the town in hopes of catching a glimpse — which
is both a business boon and a headache for

00:04:56.820 --> 00:05:01.120
locals, especially when explosive scenes are
being shot nearby one of the neighborhoods.

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:07.270
To compensate for the troubles, though, some
families are paid a monthly stipend of $400,

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:10.830
and others have received in-person thanks
from some of the cast.

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:12.560
Earning outrage

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:16.460
While plenty of devastating character deaths
have happened on The Walking Dead over the

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:20.060
years, one killing in particular had commentators
in a tizzy.

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:24.520
In the sixth season, Merritt Wever's Dr. Denise
Cloyd was killed off.

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:28.570
And it wasn't just the fact that she died
in a way that, in the comics, happened to

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:29.570
Abraham.

00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:33.510
Instead, it was the fact that her death added
to a growing trend of that season in which

00:05:33.510 --> 00:05:39.050
lesbian characters were routinely and unceremoniously
executed on various shows.

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:43.520
The show was immediately panned after the
episode aired for playing into the "bury your

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:48.350
gays" trope that seemed to be so common in
mainstream television in 2016.

00:05:48.350 --> 00:05:52.980
Of the controversy, Wever herself told The
Daily Beast, "I hadn't thought about it that

00:05:52.980 --> 00:05:53.980
way.

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:56.990
… I'm not sure that that's what was going
on here but I understand the sentiment very

00:05:56.990 --> 00:05:57.990
well."

00:05:57.990 --> 00:05:59.610
Avoiding the amputation

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:03.630
One of the most glaring omissions from The
Walking Dead's transformation from book to

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:07.330
screen has been the fact that Rick's still
got both of his hands.

00:06:07.330 --> 00:06:12.389
In the comics, The Governor cuts off Rick's
right hand — his shooter side, no less.

00:06:12.389 --> 00:06:16.580
So when the Governor arrived on-screen in
the third season, many readers were braced

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:17.949
for the inevitable.

00:06:17.949 --> 00:06:18.949
But it never happened.

00:06:18.949 --> 00:06:23.120
There have been a couple minor winks to the
event, like Merle — a character unique to

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:27.680
the show — having to cut off his own hand
to escape being handcuffed to a rooftop.

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:31.860
And then there was the time the villainous
Negan threatened to cut off Carl's hand in

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:33.330
the seventh season.

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:36.800
But Rick's still working with two fully functional
fists.

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:37.800
So what gives?

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:43.320
In his Reddit AMA series, the comic book's
co-creator Robert Kirkman explained the decision

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:46.610
as a matter of practicality, and the simple
of filming a TV show: saying:

00:06:46.610 --> 00:06:50.230
"To clarify, I think cutting Rick's hand [off]
when we did was GREAT for the comic.

00:06:50.230 --> 00:06:54.550
It's just that in another medium it would
be harder to pull off, we cheat in the comic

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:55.900
because things aren't moving.

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:57.680
You can't do that on the show.

00:06:57.680 --> 00:07:01.520
You'd see Rick not being able to reload his
gun, and things like that.

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:06.199
The CGI of cutting off Rick's hand would be
expensive, but we did it with Hershel's leg

00:07:06.199 --> 00:07:09.870
so if we felt strongly about Rick losing a
hand, we'd do it."

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:11.860
Optimistic end game

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:17.100
The show may have diverged from writer Robert
Kirkman's ongoing comic series in some significant

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:21.600
ways, but he still has a lot of creative influence
on The Walking Dead production.

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:26.130
According to him, fans can expect the ending
to both versions to be hopeful.

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:31.600
He said, "It's a very popular show, and [the
executives at AMC] seem to want it to go for

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:32.600
50 seasons.

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:37.120
And it may go for 50 seasons, but there is
definitely an end point at some point…

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:42.360
I see the story from beginning to end, over
many, many years, so I think it's a very hopeful

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:47.370
story about humanity overcoming this insurmountable,
apocalyptic situation.

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:49.670
… It's just gonna take them a long time
to do it."

00:07:49.670 --> 00:07:52.930
But until then,we'll all just enjoy the grim
ride.

00:07:52.930 --> 00:07:54.229
Thanks for watching!

00:07:54.229 --> 00:07:57.150
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:57.150 --> 00:07:59.390
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

